**TREASURER VACANCY**

The Trustees for the Mount Vernon Public Library are seeking applicants to fill the position of Library Treasurer.

The Mount Vernon Public Library Board of Trustees currently seeks a dynamic and visionary leader as the Treasurer. Under the general supervision of the Library Board of Trustees, the Treasurer serves as the Chief Financial Officer responsible for the day-to-day administration and management of the library. The Library Director will be the active public face of the Library.

The incumbent must be a visionary with strategic and tactical approaches to:

● Oversees payroll, accounts payable, financial reporting and control;

● Ensures the presentation of timely and meaningful financial reports to the Board;

● Prepares and manages line item budget for the library;

● Responsible for the accurate and efficient management of all financial operations of the library ensuring that effective procedures have been established and in line with the best practice and legal requirements;

● Processes all inter-account bank transfers and sets up appropriate systems of payment;

● Presents the recommendations of the auditor to the Board for their approval. When the Finance Committee reviews the results of the audit including the management letter, develops a plan or recommendation, if necessary, and presents the results to the Board; Leads the Board in assuring compliance with Federal, State, and other reporting requirements,

● Monitors grant reporting and appropriate release of temporarily restricted funds;

● Assists Library Director with the development of annual and program budgets;

● Reviews incoming and outgoing invoices;

● Oversees expense allocations;

● Oversees and reviews the work of the Chief Accountant Clerk and/or Principal Clerk;

● Monitors and makes recommendations for asset retirement and replace;

● Reviews, revises, and maintains internal accounting controls and procedures;

● Reviews all financial reports;

● Prepares RPS for auditing services;

● Oversees Audit Procedures;

● Prepares monthly and year-end financial reports;

● Attends all monthly and special meetings and working sessions;

● Reviews all financial reports;

If selected, the Candidate will have to take the Civil Service Exam when scheduled.

The mission of the Mount Vernon Public Library is to provide a safe, accessible facility where people, information, and ideas come together to enrich lives and build community, and where lifelong habits of learning, self-improvement and self –expression are championed. As the Central Library of Westchester, the Mount Vernon Public Library focuses on developing unique and current collections that build on technological advances, serving the diversity of patrons throughout the county.

The Mount Vernon Public Library is guided by the following principles to achieve excellence: support for intellectual freedom, literacy promotion, respect for and inclusion of the entire community, fostering a healthy democracy, forming strong partnerships, adaptability, innovation, and a professional and skilled staff that serves people of all ages, interests and abilities with fairness and equality.

**DISTINGUISHING FEATURES OF CLASS**: The incumbent in this class is chief financial administrator of the Library. The work involves carrying out broad policy as determined by the Library Board of Trustees. Supervision is exercised over the work of subordinate supervisors, including professional and clerical personnel, except the Chief Accountant Clerk and/or Principle Clerk. The Treasurer reports to the Board of Trustees.

**REQUIRED KNOWLEDGES, SKILLS ABILITIES** Good knowledge of methods used in keeping financial accounts and records; some knowledge of the laws, regulations, procedures and policies as they related to library finances; ability to learn ADP or any type of timekeeping software; good accounting judgement; ability to follow complex oral and written directions; ability to prepare correspondence, reports, and other materials; integrity; honesty; good judgement; mental alertness; clerical aptitude; tact and courtesy; ability to get along with well with others and physical conditions condition commensurate with the demands of the position.

**ACCEPTABLE TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE:**

(A). Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration or Accounting from a recognized four-year college. PLUS

(B) Five years of accounting or general business experience which shall have involved keeping auditing and financial records.

Applications submitted prior to November 15th will be given priority consideration. The salary is commensurate with experience. Salary will commensurate with experience.

Candidates interested in this position should forward cover letter, resume and salary requirements to the Personnel Committee at trustee4@mtvplibrary.org

The MVPL is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to achieving full and equal opportunity without regard to race, religion, color, gender, physical or mental disability and sexual orientation. The MVPL has a zero tolerance for sexual harassment or reprisal.

Pay: Salary commensurate with experience.

Job Type: Full-time

To Apply: Submit your resume to: trustee4@mvplibrary.org or mail to Mt. Vernon Public Library 28 South 1stt Avenue Mt. Vernon NY 10550. Please direct questions to the Director, Timur Davis at 914 668-1840 ext. 215.

Job Type: Full-time

Pay: Up to $100,000.00 per year

Benefits:

* 401(k)
* Dental insurance
* Health insurance
* Paid time off
* Retirement plan

Work Location: In person

Senior Strategist, Commercial Strategy 
 Senior Strategists play a critical role on our teams, turning a loosely framed client question into a defined analytical problem, owning the work that answers it. On any given project, they build the models and business cases that show which ideas are worth bringing to market, what those ideas are worth, and what it will take to deliver them. They design analyses from a blank workbook, construct views of markets and business models where no clean comparable exists, direct the contributions of Strategists and Associate Strategists, and present recommendations to executive audiences alongside more senior team members. As a Senior Strategist, you will apply Proto’s approach to innovation strategy with light oversight and increasingly shape how the team practices it.
 What you will do: 
- Turn a loosely framed client question into a defined analytical problem, breaking it into components, identifying which ones are load bearing, and framing two or three approaches before the work starts;
- Expect a first approach to break, treat each failed attempt as information, and return with what was learned and the next variant in hand;
- Work from limited or imperfect data to build a defensible view of a market, offering, or business model when no clean comparable exists, reasoning from first principles about who pays and what the unit of scale is, triangulating from smart proxies, and sizing markets bottom up;
- Design financial and operating models from a blank workbook, matching the form of the analysis to the question and building driver based structures that mirror how the business actually works;
- Isolate and clearly label every assumption so clients and colleagues can follow the logic and pressure-test it, prioritize the variables that actually drive business impact, and avoid getting lost in analysis for analysis’s sake;
- Pull, clean, join, and segment client data in Python, including unstructured inputs such as free text CRM notes, and sanity check findings against reality before presenting them;
- Convert analyses that worked into parameterized models, dashboards, or scripted pipelines that clients can run and maintain after the engagement ends;
- Synthesize learnings into clear and actionable strategic deliverables that lead with the answer and hold up under a hostile read, and present them to executive audiences with internal and client teams, defending the argument without the deck when needed;
- Collaborate with, and take input from brand, innovation, and experience strategists, engagement managers, designers, and clients from different backgrounds;
- Arrive at working sessions with a draft of the answer, what you have ruled out, and where you want input, and share work at 60 percent confidence so the team can shape it early;
- Direct the contributions of Strategists and Associate Strategists on your workstream, review their work for logic and rigor before it reaches the client, and turn what each engagement taught you into methods and assets the team reuses.
 Qualifications 
- 4-7 years of client side or consulting experience in corporate strategy, growth strategy, or new venture development, owning the analysis behind growth, business model, or investment decisions and presenting it to executive audiences;
- Undergraduate and/or graduate degree in economics, finance, engineering, business administration, accounting, or related disciplines preferred;
- Experience working with large and messy data sets to identify insights and commercial opportunities;
- An advanced command of Excel and financial modeling, with a track record of building models from scratch that others could audit;
- Working fluency in Python and comfort with AI assisted building such as Claude Cowork or Claude Code (bonus: a client tool or dashboard you have shipped);
- Comfortable working with collaboration tools and communication platforms (Slack, Google Suite, AI, Figma, etc.) and willing to experiment with new ones;
- Comfortable moving forward amidst ambiguity, working with imperfect data sets, and getting functionally conversant in a new industry within days;
- Based in New York metro area;
- Willing to travel up to 25% for client meetings.
 In New York City, the base salary for this position is $120k-135k, and Proto’s compensation packages include other competitive offerings. Individual compensation varies based on job-related factors including business needs, years of relevant experience, level of responsibility and qualifications.
 Proto is a New York-based company with offices at 120 Broadway, 34th floor. Our staff is encouraged to work-from-office on days of their choosing based on personal preferences, collaboration moments, client meetings, and all-company gatherings. We also support workplace flexibility and have made work-from-anywhere available to all staff (within a 3-hour time zone of eastern standard time zone). Our core business hours are generally 9:30am-6:00pm EST; however, due to our client service model and collaborative working culture, individual working hours fluctuate to reflect client deadlines and deliverables.
